{"conditionalSetIds":[],"forecasterId":"demographics-ai-2036:run2:labor:reconciler","informationSetArtifactId":"sha256:cce5ce816e44ef5fd04dcf5148d56f0f1422834af930942473986fe7182b7a0c","modelForecastIds":[],"modelUse":"none","prediction":{"kind":"categorical","probabilities":{"A":0.19,"B":0.5,"C":0.18,"D":0.13}},"questionHash":"sha256:ca2a4311940635fba34c40e7278721deb2f4716732e6011c94e6eb0554263e61","questionId":"demographics-ai-2036-cq6","questionVersion":"1.0.0","rationale":"GROWTH MARGINAL, read strictly off MY OWN CQ3 (P10 0.9 / P50 1.75 / P90 3.0; two-piece normal, sigma_up 0.98, sigma_down 0.66): P(g >= 2.6) = 0.19; P(g < 2.0) = 0.60; P(g < 1.7) = 0.47. INFLATION MARGINAL for 2032-36, derived from MY OWN CQ2: conjunct A's 0.60 for >= 2.50% on the 2027-36 mean with 2027-29 at ~2.70% implies a later sub-window central of 2.40% with sigma 0.52. PROFILE ARBITRATION: Fermi argues a RISING profile (care Baumol, non-tradable labour scarcity and the interest claim strengthen monotonically as the old-age ratio goes 31% -> 40%, while Chinese goods deflation and AI services deflation are front-loaded); Scout and the Red-Teamer argue FRONT-LOADED (the observed 3.6% core and >10% energy inflation near-lock 2027-29, so the later window is cooler). I side ~60/40 with front-loaded, because an observed starting level is a fact and monotone strengthening is a model, but I keep Fermi's terms as a floor that prevents a return to target — hence 2.40%, between the Bayesian's 2.45 and the Red-Teamer's 2.40 and below Fermi's 2.55. P(core >= 2.7) = 0.28; P(core < 2.0) = 0.22. LEXICAL LOCK, FIRST MATCH WINS. STEP 1: A = P(g >= 2.6) = 0.19 -> 19. CONSISTENCY CHECK AGAINST MY CQ3, EXPLICITLY: my P50 is 1.75% and my P90 is 3.0%, so A is a right-tail event and 19 is exactly the mass my own stated quantiles place above 2.6 — the lock's worked example (a P50 of 2.1% forbidding most mass on A) is satisfied a fortiori. Rule 1 is a pure growth test so I do not haircut for A's qualitative clauses; since my CQ1 of 14 says broad wage gains are unlikely, 19 is an UPPER BOUND on the substantive regime. If the Red-Team's China correction is wrong and China runs at Fermi's 1.97%, coupled growth falls ~0.3 pp and A collapses to ~11, with the mass going to B and D. STEP 2: C = P(core >= 2.7 AND g < 2.0). Unconditional 0.60 x 0.28 = 0.168; I raise the conditional to 0.31 for the supply-wall co-occurrence Scout documents (energy inflation already above 10%, the US electrician deficit ~107,000 peaking 2027 against BLS shortfalls of ~81,000/yr THROUGH 2034, care vacancies clearing by rationing under Baumol against a strained administered payer), which makes low growth and high core inflation the SAME event rather than opposing ones; offset downward because the capex-bust branch produces low growth with LOW inflation and populates D instead. 0.60 x 0.31 = 0.186 -> C = 18. C is DERIVED from my CQ2, not asserted: my OECD-only marginal of 0.60 applies to >= 2.50% on the full 2027-36 mean, while C needs the tighter >= 2.70% on the later, cooler sub-window AND simultaneous sub-2.0% growth, so C must sit far below 0.60 — it does. Sensitivity: Fermi's rising-profile central of 2.55 would give C = 21, the Red-Teamer's read would give C = 17, so the answer is insensitive to the arbitration within +/-3 points. STEP 3: D = P(g < 1.7 AND core < 2.0), disjoint from C by construction. Unconditional 0.47 x 0.22 = 0.103; conditional raised to 0.28 for the AI-Q4 impairment branch landing as deflationary digestion, BIS AER 2026 Box C's labour-income demand deficit, and imported Chinese goods deflation (my own CQ2 conjunct B at 0.68). 0.47 x 0.28 = 0.132 -> D = 13. I hold D BELOW the Bayesian's 15 and far below Scout's 22 on the Red-Teamer's best analytic point outside CQ3: AI-Q4 is DISJUNCTIVE and its second disjunct (net external AI revenue < 0.5x annualized compute D&A for two consecutive years) is close to an accounting tautology during a buildout with short GPU service lives, so a 66% AI-Q4 carries far less information about capital destruction or a 2032-36 demand shortfall than Fermi and Scout propagated into their D cells. A correctly RAISED AI-Q4 is compatible with higher coupled growth, not lower. STEP 4: B = residual = 100 - 19 - 18 - 13 = 50. SUM = 100 exactly. TAXONOMY NOTE, extending Fermi's and the Red-Teamer's: my CQ3 P50 of 1.75% sits just INSIDE B's own stated 1.7-2.5% band, so unlike the Fermi (1.5%), Scout (1.6%) and Bayesian (1.6%) payloads, my modal cell's label roughly matches my central growth rate. That is a warning about aggregating this effort, not a virtue of mine: three of the five payloads put ~44-50 points in a cell whose label overstates their own growth forecast by ~0.5-1.0 pp, so an unweighted average of the CQ6 vectors across this effort recovers a B that most panelists do not actually hold.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:56.223Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"An official medium-term China projection (IMF WEO or World Bank China Economic Update) places 2032-36 average annual real growth below 2.50%/yr, with no PPP benchmark reclassification explaining it; or China's realized 2028-31 average prints below 3.0%/yr on IMF WEO data.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031 (WEO vintage covering 2032-36) / Jun 30, 2032 for the realized check\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"My 2.75% China leg -- the single largest move I made off the Wave-2 posterior, and the one that rests on a borrowed red-team attack rather than on my own arithmetic -- is wrong, and Fermi's bottom-up 1.97% stands after all. CQ3 P50 falls from 1.75% to ~1.50% and P90 from 3.0 to ~2.7; CQ6-A falls from 19 to ~11 with ~5 points to B and ~3 to D; CQ4 P50 falls ~15 bp to ~2.15% via the g term; plank (d) falls from 16 to ~11. This is the cleanest single falsifier of my payload.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Published OECD or national-statistical-office sectoral earnings data (not a job board) show cumulative real median hourly wage growth in ISIC F+Q exceeding ISIC J+K+M by at least +4.5 percentage points over 2025-2030 -- on pace for the +10.0 pp threshold -- with the gap widening and NOT attributable to F+Q composition shifting toward physicians.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031 (2030 reference-year releases)\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"My conjunct-B marginal of 0.22 is too low and the care shortfall is clearing by PRICE, which is the hinge of my whole effort. CQ1 moves from 14 to ~26-30; plank (a) moves from 6 to ~20; CQ6-C gains ~5 points from B as the administered-wage Baumol inflation channel goes live; my CQ2 conjunct-A marginal rises from 0.60 to ~0.70, taking CQ2 to ~45. The mirror branch is equally informative: a gap below +2.0 pp by end-2031 means the Red-Teamer's within-F+Q composition leg was wrong, CQ1 falls to ~9, and the Bayesian's 0.105 was right despite its double-counted likelihood ratios.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Statutory minimum nurse or care staffing ratios are suspended, waived, indefinitely delayed or repealed on fiscal or workforce-availability grounds in at least three of {United States (CMS), Japan, Germany, Korea, United Kingdom}.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2030\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"CONFIRMS my decision to discount the Red-Teamer's ratio-mandate mechanism to roughly a third of his weight rather than adopting it, so CQ1 stays near 14 and does not need revising downward. The falsifying branch is the mirror: if all five jurisdictions hold their mandates AND at least two enforce them with funded rate increases, the quantity constraint has become a price obligation, CQ1 rises to ~24, CQ6-C gains ~5 points, and my 0.22 on conjunct B was the error.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"GDP-weighted OECD-38 core CPI/PCE, published on a consistent weighted basis by the OECD or BIS, prints below 2.00%/yr for four consecutive quarters at any point before mid-2031.\",\"by_when\":\"Jun 30, 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"The 2027-29 arithmetic lock-in that carries my CQ2 to 39 evaporates, and Scout's self-flagged unpublished ~2.8-3.1% weighted level was simply wrong. CQ2 falls from 39 to ~22; the 2032-36 core central falls from 2.40% to ~1.90%, moving CQ6-C from 18 to ~7 and CQ6-D from 13 to ~21; plank (c) rises from 32 to ~58; CQ4 P50 falls ~25 bp as the inflation-risk component of the term premium deflates, and CQ5 conjunct A falls from 0.42 to ~0.30, taking CQ5 to ~14.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"In the next MSCI World peak-to-trough drawdown of at least 15%, G7 GDP-weighted 10-year nominal sovereign yields measured from the EQUITY PEAK to the EQUITY TROUGH fall by at least 100 bps, on benchmark closes.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"The Red-Teamer's re-dating hit -- the one Wave-2 argument I adopted nearly in full on CQ5 -- does not survive contact, and the historical 3-of-8 flight-to-quality split was correctly classified after all. CQ5 falls from 20 to ~13 (conjunct B from 0.34 to ~0.22); CQ4's P90 falls from 3.6 to ~3.3 as the non-hedging/term-premium regime recedes; CQ6-C loses ~2 points to B. Conversely, nominals RISING by 25 bps or more through such a window would confirm the re-dating and take CQ5 to ~28 with CQ4 P50 up ~15 bp.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run2 wave 3 reconciler seat, effort 'labor'."}}